    AM-004 Automatic Depreciation Entries: Scheduled Action.

    Per AAP Rule R-06 (MUST: ir.cron via XML for AM-004 and PF-002),
    this scheduled job is declared as an XML record (model="ir.cron")
    rather than a Python-level scheduling primitive. The cron entry
    point is the @api.model method
    account.asset._cron_post_depreciation_entries which:

      * Searches for all open assets with at least one due draft
        depreciation line.
      * Posts each due line via the depreciation-line model's
        action_post method (which creates a balanced
        account.move and (conditionally on the asset category's
        auto_post_depreciation flag) posts it).
      * Auto-closes assets whose net book value has reached the
        salvage value (AM-004 AC6 "Fully Depreciated Asset").
      * Logs structured INFO / WARNING / EXCEPTION records for
        observability.
      * Returns a dict {success, skipped, errors} of per-line
        and per-asset counters.

    Wrapped in <data noupdate="1"> so administrator customization
    of the schedule (interval, active flag, user) is preserved
    across module upgrades.

    Visibility: after install, the cron is reachable at
    Settings > Technical > Automation > Scheduled Actions
    under the name "AM-004: Post Asset Depreciation Entries".
-->
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="1">

        <!--
            Cron user: defaults to the OdooBot internal user
            (base.user_root) so the cron always runs with
            administrative privileges and never depends on a
            still-active human user. This matches the precedent set
            by Odoo core's addons/account/data/service_cron.xml
            scheduled actions.

            Interval: daily at 03:00 server time. Daily cadence
            ensures depreciation entries are posted on or shortly
            after their scheduled date; running once per day is
            sufficient because the cron is idempotent (re-runs are
            no-ops for already-posted lines).

            state="code" mode invokes the Python expression in
            "code" against "model", where "model" is the
            recordset of account.asset (the model_id reference
            below). The recordset is empty at cron-trigger time, so
            model._cron_post_depreciation_entries() invokes the
            @api.model method directly.

            numbercall defaults to -1 (unlimited) and
            priority defaults to 5 (low priority) so the cron
            does not pre-empt time-critical accounting jobs.
        -->
        <record id="ir_cron_asset_depreciation" model="ir.cron">
            <field name="name">AM-004: Post Asset Depreciation Entries</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="model_account_asset"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">model._cron_post_depreciation_entries()</field>
            <field name="user_id" ref="base.user_root"/>
            <field name="interval_number">1</field>
            <field name="interval_type">days</field>
            <field name="active" eval="True"/>
            <field name="priority">5</field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
